WEBVTT

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.686
I procrastinated for about three years.

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:04.400
I tried to write
a more normal novel instead,

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.866
because I thought it was just too batty.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:09.636
AG: Too batty, really?

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:11.899
MA: Yeah, I mean it
doesn't seem very batty now.

00:11:11.923 --> 00:11:13.256
But think of when this was.

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:14.896
It was in the early '80s.

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:17.866
Yeah, it just seemed a bit too batty.

00:11:17.890 --> 00:11:21.166
AG: Margaret wasn't just worried
that the plot was far-fetched.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:24.702
Her fears actually kept her
from writing the book sooner.

00:11:24.726 --> 00:11:26.797
MA: You don't know who's going to read it.

00:11:26.821 --> 00:11:28.026
You've got no idea.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:30.193
You don't know
whether they'll like it or not.